ESG integration considers financially relevant environmental, social, and governance factors in risk and value analysis.|Poor safety controls create disruption, fines, and employee turnover.|ESG integration guarantees higher returns?|No|Yes|Only with high ratings
Sustainability reporting communicates relevant impacts and risks under a stated framework; materiality definitions differ.|Investor-focused financial materiality differs from broader impact materiality.|All frameworks use identical materiality?|No|Yes|Only for listed firms
Physical climate risk concerns damage and disruption; transition risk concerns policy, technology, and demand changes.|Flooding affects a factory; carbon policy affects operating costs.|These are respectively…?|Physical and transition risks|Both only physical|Both only transition
Green bonds specify eligible use of proceeds; sustainability-linked finance links terms to agreed performance targets.|A linked loan changes pricing if a target is missed.|A green label guarantees low credit risk?|No|Yes|Only for sovereign issuers
Carbon pricing assigns costs to emissions; markets trade specified allowances or credits with quality differences.|Assumed ₹50 carbon price × 100 tonnes adds ₹5,000 cost.|Every carbon credit has identical integrity?|No|Yes|Only if traded
Impact investing seeks measurable social or environmental outcomes alongside financial objectives.|A lender measures borrower outcomes rather than merely counting loans.|Activity counts alone prove additional impact?|No|Yes|Only at large scale
Blended finance combines concessional and commercial resources to address barriers under explicit risk allocation.|Public first-loss support attracts private funding.|Subsidy alone proves additionality and good value?|No|Yes|Only for infrastructure
Financial inclusion improves suitable access and usage; affordability, protection, and outcomes matter.|New accounts remain unused or incur excessive fees.|Account count alone establishes successful inclusion?|No|Yes|Only digitally
Stewardship uses voting, engagement, and escalation to influence investee behaviour.|An investor seeks stronger disclosure and board accountability.|Engagement outcomes should be…?|Tracked against explicit objectives|Assumed successful|Ignored after a meeting
Greenwashing overstates sustainability; weak data and conflicting methodologies limit conclusions.|A fund's label conflicts with holdings and measurable claims.|Best response?|Inspect definitions, evidence, and consistency|Trust the label|Use one score blindly
Islamic finance applies Shariah principles, including restrictions on riba and prohibited activities, with contract-specific governance.|A financing structure uses a permissible asset transaction rather than an interest loan.|A product name alone proves compliance?|No|Yes|Only if Arabic
Murabaha is cost-plus sale; ijara lease; musharaka partnership; mudaraba capital-management partnership; sukuk represent structured interests.|An ijara structure earns rent from an eligible asset under its terms.|Sukuk are universally identical to unsecured conventional bonds?|No|Yes|Only if tradable
Cooperative and community finance use member or local participation with governance and shared objectives.|Members pool savings and approve lending within agreed rules.|Community ownership removes credit and governance risk?|No|Yes|Only for small groups
Nonprofit and endowment finance supports mission, restrictions, spending, liquidity, and sustainability.|Restricted donations cannot automatically fund unrelated operations.|Total cash equals unrestricted spending capacity?|No|Yes|Only for charities
